---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Panta — Digital presence that actually works"
  description="Panta helps small businesses, nonprofits, and independent practices get found, trusted, and chosen online. Start with a Digital Presence Audit: 10 days, flat price, prioritized fix list."
>
  <section class="section section--dark hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="label">Digital business consulting</p>
      <h1>Your customers need to find you, trust you, and choose you.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Panta helps small businesses, nonprofits, and independent practices fix
        the places online where that path breaks — with strategy and
        engineering from the same hands.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a href="/audit/" class="btn btn--primary">Get your Digital Presence Audit</a>
        <a href="#how-it-works" class="btn btn--ghost">See how it works</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="how-it-works">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="label">The arc we audit</p>
      <h2>Every customer, client, and donor follows the same path.</h2>
      <p>
        Wherever someone meets you — Google, a directory, a friend's
        recommendation they go verify — three things have to go right. Most
        organizations are leaking at one of them and can't see which.
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid--3" style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
        <div class="card">
          <p class="card__kicker">Find</p>
          <h3>Can they find you?</h3>
          <p>
            Search results, Google Business Profile, maps, directories, social.
            Gaps and inconsistencies here mean people who need you never know
            you exist.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <p class="card__kicker">Trust</p>
          <h3>Do they believe you?</h3>
          <p>
            Reviews, consistent information, a recognizable brand, signs of
            life. People check — and quietly move on when what they find looks
            stale or contradictory.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <p class="card__kicker">Choose</p>
          <h3>Can they choose you?</h3>
          <p>
            A clear next step, a form that works on a phone, a reply that comes
            fast. This is where most of the money leaks — and the cheapest
            place to fix it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--bamboo">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="label">The first step</p>
      <h2>The Digital Presence Audit</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="max-width: 56ch;">
        In 10 business days, know exactly where your presence is working, where
        it's broken, and what to fix first — with a 90-day roadmap that
        separates what you can do yourself from what's worth hiring out.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
        <a href="/audit/" class="btn btn--primary" style="background: var(--charcoal); color: var(--cream);">What's in the audit</a>
        <span style="font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 1.1rem;">
          $950 flat &nbsp;·&nbsp; founding clients $750 &nbsp;·&nbsp; nonprofits 15% off
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="label">Who we work with</p>
      <h2>Built for organizations that are excellent at what they do — and invisible where people look.</h2>
      <div class="grid grid--3" style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Nonprofits &amp; community organizations</h3>
          <p>
            Donors, volunteers, and funders all vet you online before they say
            yes. We audit each path separately — and check whether you're using
            the $10k/month Google Ad Grant you may already qualify for.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Professional practices</h3>
          <p>
            Therapists, consultants, attorneys. New clients decide on
            directories and Google before your website ever loads. We audit
            what your ethics code actually allows — no advice you can't use.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Small business &amp; e&#8209;commerce</h3>
          <p>
            From the map pack to the checkout flow. Site speed, reviews,
            abandoned carts, and the follow-through systems that turn being
            found into being paid.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="label">Why Panta</p>
      <h2>Strategy and engineering, from the same hands.</h2>
      <div class="grid grid--2" style="margin-top: 2rem; gap: 2.5rem;">
        <div>
          <p>
            Most consultants hand you a report and wish you luck. Most
            developers build what they're told without asking whether it's the
            right thing. Panta is one practice that does both: we diagnose what's
            broken, and we can build the fix — custom tools included.
          </p>
          <p>
            Every recommendation is backed by something we can actually build.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>
            And we'll tell you the truth: about a third of every roadmap we
            deliver is stuff you can do yourself, free, with the guides we
            include. The honesty is the point — it's how you know the rest is
            worth paying for.
          </p>
          <p style="font-family: var(--font-serif); font-style: italic; font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--sage);">
            "Here's the one thing to fix first."
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
        <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn--primary">Book a free 20-minute call</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
